    "scenesThatPass": [
      "MORWENNA: All those herbs that we picked? We’re going to make tea into your favorite cup.\nBIRDY: It is my favorite cup.\nMORWENNA: I know.\nMORWENNA: And swirl and dip.",
      "BIRDY: Mumma!\nAISLINN: Well I, for one, should like my room free of jesters for the moment. I should like to rest and do my puzzles.",
      "AELIS: Your hair is so long Birdy. You need to brush it.\nBIRDY: I’m going to grow it all the way down to my feet.",
      "BERENICE: Well, I go where I want and I say what I please.\nAELIS: She’s been writing the most tragic poetry.",
      "BIRDY: As the time approaches when I must wed, I must undertake lady lessons. My two least favorite words. Together. In one terrible phrase.\nCORNETHIA: Gently, young ladies. A gentle hand plays a soothing tune.\nBIRDY: Sister Cornethia attempts to make me musical, pious, and full of grace for any suitor who may court.\nCORNETHIA: Do we find our lessons ever so funny? Seems to me a joke is astir."
    ]
  },
